{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqgu1e5450o","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"CDX-2 judge: APPROVED — Codex→config.toml + every .mcp.json writer merges; both client identities coexist","summary":"Reviewed attempt orch/attempt/fbeb4c89-...-3 (commit c594a61) in single-attempt code-review mode and merged it into orch/feature/codex-parity (merge head 50f1bbcb, clean no-ff). Verified every core claim against the code, not just the summary:\n(1) Codex MCP now routes to ~/.codex/config.toml under [mcp_servers.orchestrator-graph] (TOML, command=node, args=[INSTALL_DIR/mcp-graph.js], env ORCH_PORT + ORCH_CLIENT=\"codex\") via writeCodexMcp(); the old writeCodexMcp(cwd,...) that wrote <cwd>/.mcp.json is gone and wireHarness('codex') calls writeCodexMcp() with the default homedir path — Codex no longer clobbers the repo .mcp.json.\n(2) Hand-rolled TOML strip (stripCodexOrchTable) is correct on the flagged edge case: `dropping` is recomputed on EVERY header line, so a sibling [mcp_servers.*] table appearing AFTER the orchestrator block survives (the loop pushes the sibling header the moment dropping flips false). Sibling [mcp_servers.other] + unrelated [features] preserved; re-run yields exactly one orchestrator-graph table (verified by test). [[array.table]] double-bracket headers are matched and preserved for non-orch names.\n(3) writeMcp is now read-modify-write merge (sets mcpServers[\"orchestrator-graph\"], preserves user-added servers, backs up .bak once, mkdir -p, forward-slashed path). checkMcp path-check made fwd-slash-aware so a correct Windows entry isn't re-flagged.\n(4) REGRESSION CLEARED — cursor still gets ORCH_CLIENT=\"cursor\": wireHarness('cursor')→checkMcp(cwd,'cursor')→writeMcp(...,'cursor')→orchestratorMcpEntry('cursor') sets env.ORCH_CLIENT='cursor'. Removing dead injectOrchClient did NOT drop cursor identity; a dedicated test asserts it.\n(5) --harness parses comma-separated AND repeatable, de-duped, default ['claude']; init loops wireHarness over all selected; printNextSteps per harness.\n(6) Regression tests are MEANINGFUL not vacuous — assert BOTH identities survive (Claude in .mcp.json with no ORCH_CLIENT, Codex in config.toml with ORCH_CLIENT=\"codex\"), ","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-16T16:04:23.128Z","vec":[-0.09574408829212189,0.001258460571989417,0.02063041552901268,-0.019189581274986267,-0.02135622687637806,-0.05966859683394432,-0.016255764290690422,0.03384357690811157,-0.022655067965388298,0.05054032430052757,0.06182011589407921,0.00017247935466002673,0.07297497242689133,-0.07210711389780045,-0.00880683958530426,0.03233040124177933,-0.0030330088920891285,0.035059522837400436,-0.017534494400024414,0.002396815223619342,-0.05870863422751427,-0.038139864802360535,-0.02320583537220955,-0.022318145260214806,0.016217291355133057,0.01895713247358799,0.004642703104764223,-0.018156040459871292,-0.08116893470287323,-0.008933152072131634,-0.032830867916345596,0.15386269986629486,-0.11868871003389359,0.006373899057507515,0.1062365472316742,0.12123490869998932,0.014190608635544777,-0.024029353633522987,-0.04046093299984932,-0.06328880041837692,0.023125948384404182,0.07115287333726883,-0.04497530311346054,0.0064790635369718075,-0.0585450753569603,-0.06605605781078339,-0.056546133011579514,-0.048354946076869965,-0.07375585287809372,0.0032023703679442406,-0.04388163238763809,0.04554927349090576,0.011513550765812397,0.014131800271570683,0.09051383286714554,0.02997097559273243,-0.03727051988244057,0.034581445157527924,-0.01400102861225605,0.026370909065008163,-0.020679865032434464,0.009081684052944183,-0.07162687927484512,0.01547629851847887,0.01259713526815176,0.04380359128117561,-0.009456359781324863,0.009605737403035164,0.0022252106573432684,0.020832331851124763,-0.0021786517463624477,0.026109598577022552,-0.08811336755752563,0.016162078827619553,-0.027772972360253334,0.07775648683309555,0.05012534558773041,0.03590201959013939,-0.0019358276622369885,-0.15593808889389038,-0.06100384145975113,0.008977176621